			(at 0 0 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "Fanstel BT840 -- Nordic nRF52840 BLE 5 module, Cortex-M4F 64MHz, 1MB flash, 256KB RAM, integrated PCB trace antenna, on-module DC-DC. 14 x 16 x 1.9mm. VDD 1.7-3.6V. HYBRID PACKAGE: 16 castellated pins (numbered 1-16) plus LGA pads (Z0-Z6, A0-A6, B0-B6, C0-C6, D0-D6, E0-E6, F0-F6). The datasheet says SMT is not required for the castellated pins alone, but a design needing more than ~14 signals must use the LGA pads and reflow the part. PIN COUNT: 65 modelled (16 castellated + 49 LGA). The datasheet summary says '16 castellated and 45 LGA', which appears to count only the small signal pads: F0-F3 are listed in its own Pin Function table as bare 'Ground pad' entries with no ball reference, and a real BT840 footprint shows them as 1.4986mm SQUARE pads, far larger than the 0.6mm circular signal LGA pads. They are physical pads that must be soldered and grounded, so they are modelled as pins. An earlier revision of this symbol wrongly dropped them to reach 61; do not repeat that. Pin names transcribed from the real Fanstel datasheet BT840/F/E/X/XE Ver 1.15 (Sep 2019) 'Pin Function' table, extracted with pdftotext -raw; the -layout mode interleaves BT840 with BT832 columns and must not be used for it. F5 DCCH is the DC-DC converter output and is typed passive, not a supply input. B4/B5/C3/D2 are plain GPIO on this variant but are PA-control pins on BT840X/XE -- avoid them if the design might ever move to a PA variant."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
